    "rich_text_czWEgw": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_kYqBzH": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Lab-Grown Diamonds: A Complete Guide",
            "use_h1": true
          }
        },
        "text_jUByfz": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Lab-grown diamonds are real diamonds created using advanced technology that replicates the natural formation process. They offer the same brilliance, durability, and chemical composition as natural diamonds, while providing a more accessible price point.</p><p>At Milano Jewelry, we offer both lab-grown and natural diamonds. Our approach is rooted in transparency—so you can make an informed decision based on your preferences, values, and budget.</p>",
            "enlarge_text": false
          }
        },
        "subheading_JXaHAf": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "subheading": "What Are Lab-Grown Diamonds?"
          }
        },
        "text_hNnGUx": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Lab-grown diamonds are formed in controlled laboratory environments using processes that mimic the conditions under which diamonds develop beneath the Earth’s surface.</p><p>They possess the same physical, chemical, and optical properties as natural diamonds. To the naked eye, they are indistinguishable from mined diamonds and can only be identified using specialized equipment.</p><p>Lab-grown diamonds are certified by leading gemological institutes such as IGI and GIA, ensuring authenticity and quality.</p>",
            "enlarge_text": false
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_kYqBzH",
        "text_jUByfz",
        "subheading_JXaHAf",
        "text_hNnGUx"
      ],
      "custom_css": [
        ".subheading {color: #002058; font-size: 20px; margin-bottom: 6px;}"
      ],
      "name": "Rich text",
      "settings": {
        "height": "small",
        "text_alignment": "left",
        "full_width": true,
        "color_scheme": "default"
      }
    },
    "rich_text_hAiEAk": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_D3QV9X": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How Lab-Grown Diamonds Are Created",
            "use_h1": false
          }
        },
        "text_cE74mh": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Lab-grown diamonds are produced using two primary methods:</p><p><strong>High Pressure High Temperature (HPHT)</strong><br/><br/>This method recreates the high-pressure, high-temperature conditions found deep within the Earth. Carbon atoms crystallize around a diamond seed, forming a diamond over time.</p><p><strong>Chemical Vapor Deposition (CVD)</strong><br/><br/>In this process, a diamond seed is placed in a chamber filled with carbon-rich gas. As the gas is energized, carbon atoms bond to the seed, building the diamond layer by layer.</p><p>Both methods result in diamonds that are chemically and structurally identical to natural diamonds.</p>",
            "enlarge_text": false
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_D3QV9X",
        "text_cE74mh"
      ],
      "custom_css": [
        ".subheading {color: #002058; font-size: 20px; margin-bottom: 6px;}"
      ],
      "name": "Rich text",
      "settings": {
        "height": "small",
        "text_alignment": "left",
        "full_width": true,
        "color_scheme": "default"
      }
    },
    "rich_text_gFfzfQ": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_qL8zf6": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Advantages of Lab-Grown Diamonds",
            "use_h1": false
          }
        },
        "text_zEze6c": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<h5>Greater Value</h5><p>Lab-grown diamonds are typically priced 30–60% lower than natural diamonds of comparable size and quality. This allows for greater flexibility in selecting higher carat weights or better clarity and color within the same budget.</p><h5>Ethical Sourcing</h5><p>Lab-grown diamonds are produced in controlled environments, offering a transparent and conflict-free alternative to traditional mining. This appeals to customers who prioritize responsible sourcing.</p><h5>Reduced Environmental Impact</h5><p>Unlike mined diamonds, lab-grown diamonds do not require large-scale excavation or land disruption. While energy is required in production, the overall environmental footprint is generally lower than that of traditional diamond mining.</p><h5>Wider Range of Options</h5><p>Lab-grown diamonds are available in a broad range of sizes, cuts, colors, and clarities. Their availability and consistency make them well-suited for both classic designs and custom jewelry.</p>",
            "enlarge_text": false
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_qL8zf6",
        "text_zEze6c"
      ],
      "custom_css": [
        ".subheading {color: #002058; font-size: 20px; margin-bottom: 6px;}"
      ],
      "name": "Rich text",
      "settings": {
        "height": "small",
        "text_alignment": "left",
        "full_width": true,
        "color_scheme": "default"
      }
    },
    "rich_text_QXRhTU": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_dz7hqA": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Considerations Before Buying",
            "use_h1": false
          }
        },
        "text_b3PXbJ": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<h3>Price Evolution</h3><p>Lab-grown diamonds follow a technology-driven pricing model. As production becomes more efficient and supply increases, prices may continue to adjust over time. They are best viewed as a purchase for personal value rather than long-term investment.</p><h3>Resale Value</h3><p>Compared to natural diamonds, lab-grown diamonds currently have lower resale value. This is influenced by market perception and supply dynamics rather than differences in quality.</p><h3>Energy Consumption</h3><p>The production of lab-grown diamonds requires significant energy, particularly in regions where fossil fuels are a primary energy source. Despite this, their overall environmental impact remains lower than traditional mining.</p><h3>Industry Impact</h3><p>The growing adoption of lab-grown diamonds has implications for regions that rely on natural diamond mining for economic activity. This is an important consideration in the broader context of the global diamond industry.</p>",
            "enlarge_text": false
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_dz7hqA",
        "text_b3PXbJ"
      ],
